# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values.
# Both values live in the Supabase dashboard:
#     - "Project URL"     → NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL        (Settings → Data API)
#     - "Publishable key" → NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   (Settings → API Keys)
#       It starts with sb_publishable_ and is safe in a browser.
#       On a project created before that panel existed there is no "API Keys" tab —
#       the same role is played by the legacy "anon public" key under
#       "Legacy API keys". Either one works here.
#
# The variable keeps its ANON_KEY name for continuity with the rest of the sprint's
# docs; "publishable key" is the current name for the same low-privilege role.
#
# NEVER put a privileged key here, or anywhere else in this project. One tab away on
# that same panel sits the key that bypasses row-level security — the replacement for
# the old service-role key. Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined textually into the
# browser bundle, so pasting that one here publishes an RLS bypass to anyone who views
# source, and the app would boot and work perfectly while doing it.
# lib/supabase/env.ts refuses it at boot — but that guard is a net, not a licence, and
# it recognises the current key format only.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
